        {
          "post_id": "484208",
          "text": "<p>Consider an undirected, weighted graph G with positive weights. Let a breadth-first traversal of G be done starting from a node r.</p><p>Let $d(r, u), d(r, v)$ represent the length of the shortest path from $r$ to $u, v$ respectively.<br><br>If u is visited before v during the traversal, which of the following must hold?</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>$d(r, u)&lt;d(r, v)$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$d(r, u) \\leq d(r, v)$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$d(r, u) \\geq d(r, v)$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>None of the above</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "subject": "Algorithms",
          "day": "Day 75"
        },
        {
