          "text": "<p>Which of the following statement(s) is/are correct?</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>Tournament method always requires fewer comparisons than linear scan for any $\\mathrm{n}&gt;2$ while finding the max and second max in an array of size $n$.<br>&nbsp;</li><li>If an array of size $n$ is sorted using bottom-up Merge Sort, then the path taken by the maximum element in the merge tree corresponds exactly to the comparisons made in the tournament method for finding the maximum.<br>&nbsp;</li><li>In a randomized tournament, the probability that the second maximum appears in the final round is $\\frac{n}{2(n-1)}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>To find the third maximum element using a tournament tree of size $n$, one may need to examine up to $\\left\\lceil\\log _2 n\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\log _2(n / 2)\\right\\rceil-1$ elements in the worst case.</li></ol>",
